            answer="The felony murder rule holds individuals liable for murder if a death occurs during the commission of a felony, regardless of intent. The misdemeanor manslaughter rule applies when a death results from a misdemeanor, typically requiring proof of recklessness or negligence, not just accidental harm. Felony murder focuses on strict liability for felony-related deaths, while misdemeanor manslaughter requires a higher showing of culpable conduct beyond mere negligence.",
