            answer="An accessory before the fact is someone who helps plan or encourage a crime before it occurs, while an accessory after the fact helps someone avoid arrest or punishment after the crime. An accessory before the fact is similar to an accomplice or someone who aids and abets, and may be considered a principal if they directly participate. A conspiracy involves an agreement to commit a crime, which can make participants accessories before the fact. For example, if someone helps plan a robbery and then encourages the perpetrator afterward to hide evidence, they are an accessory before the fact for planning and an accessory after the fact for helping hide evidence.",
